# Force LF line endings on every platform.
#
# The substrate content-addresses file BYTES (canonical-bytes + BLAKE3
# seals). The sealed L0 doctrine bundle hash (the ceremony verify_hashes
# drift gate) and the cross-language canonical-bytes test vectors are
# byte-exact, so a CRLF checkout — e.g. a Windows CI runner with
# core.autocrlf=true — would fail verify_hashes even though nothing
# changed (the bundle gains one \r per line). `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf
# so the working-tree bytes match the LF-based seal on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries — never touch their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
